<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
        The window theme, and the other half of "the app is dark everywhere".

        This used to inherit Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar. On a phone set
        to light mode that resolves to AppCompat's LIGHT theme, so the window
        underneath Compose was white while the Compose tree was drawing a
        near-black UI. That mismatch is visible in four places, all of them
        reported as "light mode looks odd":

          • the cold-start flash — the window is painted before the first Compose
            frame exists, so every launch flashed white between the splash icon
            and the app;
          • android:windowBackground shows through anywhere Compose has not
            painted yet, which includes the moment a new Activity or a
            Dialog/ModalBottomSheet window is being laid out;
          • isLightTheme=true switches the platform's own widgets — text-selection
            handles, the autofill and share sheets, the reCAPTCHA WebView chrome
            Firebase phone auth opens — to their light variants, which arrive
            light-on-light over the app's dark UI;
          • windowLightStatusBar / windowLightNavigationBar default to true under a
            light theme, i.e. dark system icons, which vanish against a bar that
            is transparent over Ink.i950.

        Theme.AppCompat.NoActionBar (no "DayNight") is permanently dark, so all
        four of those follow from the parent alone and do not need overriding
        attribute by attribute — which also keeps this file free of anything
        newer than minSdk 26.

        Do NOT add a res/values-night/ copy of this. A night variant only exists
        to differ from the day one, and there is no day one any more; adding it
        back is how the system setting leaks in again. If light mode is ever
        built, this parent and the `darkTheme` argument in ui/theme/Theme.kt have
        to change in the same commit.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Zipper" parent="Theme.AppCompat.NoActionBar">
        <!--
            Pinned to the app's own base surface rather than left at AppCompat's
            dark default (#303030, a mid grey). Compose paints ZipperColors.bgBase
            over the top, so any pixel of window still showing is a visible seam
            between two different darks — most noticeably on the launch flash and
            while the keyboard resizes the window.
        -->
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/window_bg</item>
    </style>

    <style name="Theme.Zipper.SplashScreen" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_bg</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/ic_splash_logo</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.Zipper</item>
    </style>

</resources>
